  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb (す ending, conjugates as s-row: {蒸|む}らさない, {蒸|む}らします). Transitive — takes a direct object marked with を.\n\nUSAGE:\n{蒸|む}らす is a key cooking term in Japanese cuisine. The {蒸|む}らし (steaming/resting) step after cooking rice is considered essential for achieving the ideal texture. Most Japanese rice cooker instructions include this step.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ご{飯|はん}を{蒸|む}らす (to let rice rest/steam)\n- {蓋|ふた}をして{蒸|む}らす (to cover and let steam)\n- {蒸|む}らし{時間|じかん} (steaming/resting time)\n- {五分|ごふん}{蒸|む}らす (let rest for five minutes)",
